    },
    "message": "Split long string literals to fit the line length\n\nLong single-line strings are written as implicit concatenations, split\nat spaces, after Japanese punctuation, or at replacement-field and regex\ngroup boundaries, and wrapped in parentheses where needed. Adjacent\nliterals are joined by the parser, so the AST of every file is the same\nas before and no message, source note or prompt text changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
